  "narrative": "The only due validation response is H115, the feature_063-by-feature_038 interaction. The original signed discovery estimate was +0.575 (interval +0.400 to +0.750), clearly above the 0.15-unit scientific threshold. The independent validation estimate is signed +0.329 (adjusted interval +0.086 to +0.571). Because H115 is a negative-direction interaction claim, the raw interpretation is that the feature_063 present-minus-absent difference in outcome_001 is more negative in participants with feature_038 >= 0 than in the feature_038 < 0 complement by about 0.58 composite dependency-score units in discovery and about 0.33 in validation. The validation result supports the same qualitative direction but attenuates the magnitude, and its conservative lower bound falls below the 0.15 threshold. I therefore keep H115 accepted on the combined evidence, while emphasizing that the validation establishes directional consistency more robustly than threshold-level magnitude. The next essential analysis is direct strata interpretation: feature_063 present versus absent when feature_038 is high and separately when feature_038 is low. An accepted interaction does not itself specify whether feature_063 has no effect, a weak effect, or a strong effect in each half.\n\nI also reassess H119, the reversed feature_063-by-feature_018 interaction. Its signed discovery estimate is +0.429 with interval +0.247 to +0.611, entirely above the threshold and in the registered positive direction. Rawly, this means that the feature_063 association is weaker, or less negative, when feature_018 >= 0 than in the feature_018 < 0 complement. I accept H119 but keep it active because the direct high and low feature_018 strata have not yet been tested and the claim has not yet received independent validation. H110, the originally registered negative age interaction, is now closed as rejected; the reversed age interaction H118 remains unresolved because its signed discovery estimate +0.209 has interval -0.028 to +0.445, so the lower bound does not establish threshold-level effect modification. Direct age strata are more interpretable for age: the feature_063 association is strong in participants younger than 60 but imprecise in participants 60 or older. I defer H118 relative to the higher-priority signature-interaction direct strata.\n\nThe supported dataset-specific descriptive pattern remains stable. In this supplied dataset, feature_010 presence is associated with higher outcome_001, feature_002 presence with higher outcome_001, feature_037 presence with lower outcome_001, and feature_063 presence with lower outcome_001. The three large binary labels are robust in direct presence/absence strata, and feature_063 is supported both overall and conditionally when feature_010, feature_002, and feature_037 are all absent. Feature_063 is also threshold-supported in younger participants and in the upper log progression-free survival half. Negative findings include the originally tested research markers feature_007, feature_058, and feature_015, many broad categorical and binary contrasts, the log progression-free survival interaction for feature_063, the registered negative age interaction, and the earlier opposite-direction feature_018 interaction H116 as originally written. Exact continuous high-versus-low signature formulations produced zero-cell comparisons and are invalid formulations, not scientific nulls.\n\nUnresolved uncertainty now centers on: (1) the direct feature_063 effects inside high and low halves of feature_038, feature_018, and feature_036; (2) the magnitude of H115 and H119 after direct-stratum examination and possible validation; (3) whether the possible age-dependent attenuation of feature_063 is real but imprecise; and (4) smaller feature_063 contrasts in lower log progression-free survival and in feature_010-present or feature_037-present groups. The most informative next analysis is to run H117 and the registered direct strata H120 through H125, then interpret those direct contrasts jointly with accepted interactions H115 and H119. If, as suggested by the interaction estimates, feature_063 is strongly negative in the feature_038-high and feature_018-low halves but weak or absent in their complements, this would define a dataset-specific composite dependency-score structure with stronger descriptive support. If direct strata do not match the interaction estimates, the interactions should be treated cautiously as potentially unstable or dependent on unadjusted confounding structure. All conclusions remain descriptive associations in this dataset only, not causal effects or generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Accepted dataset-specific associations: feature_010 presence higher outcome_001; feature_002 presence higher outcome_001; feature_037 presence lower outcome_001; feature_063 presence lower outcome_001. Overall feature_063 and H93 are independently validated. H115 feature_063-by-feature_038 interaction accepted: signed discovery +0.575; signed validation +0.329, adjusted lower 0.086, so direction supported but validation-alone threshold magnitude uncertain. H119 reversed feature_063-by-feature_018 interaction accepted from discovery: signed +0.429, interval +0.247 to +0.611, meaning feature_063 association is weaker/less negative when feature_018 is high; needs direct strata and later validation. H110 original negative age interaction closed rejected; H118 reversed age interaction unresolved but deferred because interval lower -0.028. H106 younger and H108 upper logPFS feature_063 contrasts accepted; H105 older and H107 lower logPFS unresolved/deferred; H109 logPFS interaction rejected. Feature_063 remains robust when feature_010/feature_002/feature_037 are absent, but conditional within feature_010-present or feature_037-present remains small-cell and unresolved. Next analysis priority: test H117 and direct feature_063 contrasts in feature_038 high/low, feature_018 high/low, and feature_036 high/low (H120-H125), then request validation for the most robust resulting interaction or direct contrast. Exact +1/-1 signature main effects and exact age contrasts remain low-priority invalid or sparse formulations. All claims are descriptive associations only."
}

