 "narrative": "No evidence assessments are due in this explore stage. The key unresolved scientific structure is the feature_063 association with outcome_001. In the supplied dataset, feature_063 presence is overall associated with a lower composite dependency score, and H93 shows that this persists when feature_010, feature_002, and feature_037 are all absent. The new central issue is whether feature_063's effect is uniform or is strongly modified by standardized research signatures. H115 supports an interaction with feature_038: the raw feature_063 present-minus-absent effect is substantially more negative when feature_038 is high than when it is low. H119, after correcting for the reversed direction, supports that the raw feature_063 effect is stronger in the feature_018-low group than in the feature_018-high group. Registered direct strata H120 through H123 will give marginal levels in each signature half, but interactions can be offsetting or confounded. Therefore I register two joint feature_063 direct contrasts that are most informative for testing the predicted interaction geometry. First, in participants with feature_038 high and feature_018 low, I expect the strongest negative raw feature_063 effect; a negative-direction claim should produce a positive signed estimate if supported. The alternative is that the interaction is spurious or that the effect is driven by only one signature, yielding a null or modest contrast. Second, in participants with feature_038 low and feature_018 high, the interactions predict a weak or near-null feature_063 effect; I register the negative direction because the overall association is negative but anticipate uncertainty. If this group remains threshold-negative, the simple interaction interpretation is incomplete. I also register refinements of H115 and H119 restricted to the population in which feature_010, feature_002, and feature_037 are absent. These clean-stratum interaction claims test whether signature-based effect modification persists when the major binary predictors are not present, reducing the possibility that the accepted interactions are artifacts of confounding by those large-effect labels. The expected directions are unchanged: more negative feature_063 effects when feature_038 is high, and less negative feature_063 effects when feature_018 is high. All hypotheses are descriptive associations in this dataset only, not causal effects or generalizable claims.",
 "research_notes": "Accepted dataset-specific associations: feature_010 presence higher outcome_001; feature_002 presence higher outcome_001; feature_037 presence lower outcome_001; feature_063 presence lower outcome_001. Overall feature_063 and H93 are independently validated. H115 feature_063-by-feature_038 interaction accepted: signed discovery +0.575; signed validation +0.329, adjusted lower 0.086, so direction supported but validation-alone threshold magnitude uncertain. H119 reversed feature_063-by-feature_018 interaction accepted from discovery: signed +0.429, interval +0.247 to +0.611; raw interpretation is feature_063 effect is less negative when feature_018 is high than when feature_018 is low. Direct H120-H123 and feature_036 strata H117/H124/H125 remain priority. New proposals add the predicted strongest joint stratum (feature_038 high and feature_018 low), predicted weak joint stratum (feature_038 low and feature_018 high), and clean-stratum refinements of H115/H119 among participants with feature_010=0, feature_002=0, feature_037=0. Interpret direct levels and interaction differences together. Next validation priority after direct/clean strata: H119 or its strongest supported refinement if threshold and direction persist. All claims remain descriptive associations only."
}
